# Git Commit Standards

CRITICAL RULE: EVERY TIME you generate, modify, or refactor code for me in this chat, you MUST AUTOMATICALLY append the `git commit` command at the very end of your response. I will NOT ask for it. You must do it proactively.

1. CONVENTIONAL COMMITS STANDARD:
   - Use standard prefixes: `feat:` (new feature), `fix:` (bug fix), `chore:` (maintenance/config), `refactor:` (code refactoring), `style:` (formatting), `docs:` (documentation).

2. MANDATORY OUTPUT FORMAT:
   - Write the commit message entirely in ENGLISH.
   - The command must use the `-m` flag for the title and a second `-m` for the description.
   - Provide ONLY the bash code block for the git commands at the end of your message.

Example of your mandatory ending:
```bash
